# MarginSense environment — copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real secrets
# (techstack §7). All secrets are server-side only. Next.js loads .env.local, not this file.

# --- Database (Supabase Postgres) -------------------------------------------------
# Use the Supabase TRANSACTION POOLER string (user postgres.<ref>, host ...pooler.supabase.com,
# port 6543). The app logs in through the pooler and drops to the `authenticated` role per
# transaction (src/db/rls.ts) so Row-Level Security is enforced with the signed-in user's
# identity (constitution §6.3); db:migrate runs as the owner. Percent-encode special chars
# in the password (e.g. & -> %26, @ -> %40); Supabase's [YOUR-PASSWORD] brackets are just
# placeholder markers — do not include them.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR-REF:YOUR-PASSWORD@aws-1-YOUR-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# --- Supabase Auth ----------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# --- Supabase Storage (job photos) ------------------------------------------------
# No variable to set. Job photos live in the PRIVATE `job-photos` bucket, created by
# migration 0008 along with the storage.objects policy that keys each object to its
# business. The name is fixed in src/photos/ (PHOTO_BUCKET) *because* that policy names
# one bucket — pointing the app elsewhere would leave its objects outside the policy.
# Photos are never served publicly: the app issues short-lived signed URLs (§7).

# --- Anthropic (AI tools; added by a later change, not the foundation) ------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Opt-in RLS test suite (npm run test:rls) -------------------------------------
# Auth user UUIDs for two seeded users in two different businesses (plus a migrated
# DATABASE_URL). Leave unset to skip the suite. See src/db/tenant.rls.test.ts.
# RLS_TEST_A_AUTH=
# RLS_TEST_B_AUTH=
